# Radharc's GPU renderer's board test (D174 section 6 step 4): the same program as boot-venus's, an app of the
# board's image, started by `echo start compose-test >/svc/launcher/ctl` (board-test does) once loinnir-test has
# ended. On a GPU whose driver host offers `csf` the renderer composes on the core's Mali backend, and a 1080p scene
# in each shipped theme is compared with the CPU renderer's and a 4K scene is timed (`theme.compose.4k`); it says
# `compose-test: ok: Radharc's GPU renderer composed on mali`. There is no Radharc beside it: it checks the
# renderer, not the desktop.
service compose-test
program compose-test
app compose-test
launcher
mount /dev devmgr/dev
mount /lib/theme bootfs/lib/theme
